210453397504	Portable device startup confirmed.\nSupport AI "Ririna," activating--
210453397505	<double><color COLOR_YELLOW>Ta-daaah!</color></double>
210453397506	From good morning to good night, the all-purpose AI\nwho supports your life: it's Ririna-chan!
210453397507	From Virtual-On advice to life counseling,\njust ask me anything!
210453397508	I will now give a controls guide for those\ntrying Virtual-On for the first time.
210453397509	Come experience the robot battles unfolding\nwith this Academy City as the field!
210453397510	Now, on to explaining each item!
210453397511	First, the basic rules of Virtual-On.
210453397512	Virtual-On is a game where you control a robot called\na Virtuaroid and fight your opponent's Virtuaroid.
210453397513	Broadly, there are 2 win conditions.
210453397514	Earn more points by the time limit,\nor destroy the enemy.
210453397515	Hitting the enemy repeatedly knocks them down.\nYou earn points by knocking the enemy down.
210453397516	The points you get depend on how you knock them\ndown, but I'll explain that another time.
210453397517	Virtual-On is a robot fighting game, but the battle of\nwits over the point lead is a real sport!
210453397518	The other win condition is simply destroying the enemy.
210453397519	Destroying means just that: attacking the enemy until\nits HP (hit points) is 0 and it can't move.
210453397520	That's a common rule in ordinary versus games, too.
210453397521	Its unique rules, combining the 2 elements of sport\nand versus game, are what define Virtual-On.
210453397522	Next, H.C.V. (Hit Clock Violation).
210453397523	If the player in the point lead goes a set time\nwithout landing an attack, an H.C.V. occurs.
210453397524	An H.C.V. deducts points.
210453397525	The time left until an H.C.V. occurs is shown\nby the time bar here.
210453397526	The H.C.V. is cleared when the point lead changes\nor the leading side lands an attack.
210453397527	If the H.C.V. isn't cleared, the time until the next\ndeduction keeps getting shorter.
210453397528	When an H.C.V. is about to occur,\nan announcement appears on screen.
210453397529	This is called the Hit Clock.
210453397530	Real sports have a tactic of scoring first and holding\nthe lead to the end, so-called "win and run," right?
210453397531	Win and run isn't fun to watch,\nso it's discouraged in Virtual-On.
210453397532	So H.C.V. is a rule to rein in win and run.\nWhen it happens, rethink how you're fighting.
210453397533	That's it for the basic explanation.
210453397534	If there's anything about the controls you don't\nunderstand, try the tutorial!
210453397535	See you again, then.\nHave a wonderful Virtual-On life!
